  "verbalization": "Fluoranthene is shown to have a target of Ataxin-2, which is in turn targeted by multiple structurally related compounds, including (1R,3R,4S,7S,9S,11S,13R,14R,15R)-4,11,13,14-tetrahydroxy-7-[(2Z,4R)-4-(hydroxymethyl)hex-2-en-2-yl]-3,9,15-trimethoxy-12,12-dimethyl-6,17-dioxabicyclo[11.3.1]heptadecan-5-one, 2,4-Bis[(4-hydroxyphenyl)methyl]-5-methoxy-3-[2-(3-methoxyphenyl)ethyl]phenol, and (2R,3S,4S,5R,6S)-2-(Hydroxymethyl)-6-[3-[(E)-3-Hydroxyprop-1-Enyl]-2,5-Dimethoxyphenoxy]Oxane-3,4,5-Triol. All these compounds share a common target of CHP-134, suggesting a potential mechanism of action involving Ataxin-2. The evidence points to a possible interaction between Fluoranthene and CHP-134 through the inhibition of Ataxin-2, which is a key target for multiple structurally diverse compounds. The presence of multiple pathways converging on Ataxin-2 and CHP-134 supports a mechanistic link, though the exact mode of action remains to be elucidated. The integration of these pathways highlights the potential for Fluoranthene to interact with CHP-134 via a shared target, but further experimental validation is required to confirm the specific mechanism and therapeutic relevance.",
